{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts","id":863979,"title":"Your Character Concepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-11T17:20:58-07:00","id":863979,"title":"Your Character Concepts","content":"Since we've got one for silly ideas, why not have one for serious ones? We could discuss them and maybe workshop them for people looking for critique/to try and improve it.<br /> <br /> I'll start with one I'm currently noodling on, a Werewolf concept that draws on some real world stuff. His name is <b>Santino Duku </b>and he's a Rahu Blood Talon that's in a pack with his &quot;adoptive family.&quot;<br /> <br /> He was one of the Lost Boys in Sudan, trekking across the country with friends after losing his family, seeing many of them die along the way as well. I imagine he had his First Change while on this trek, likely when he and his friends were attacked by SPLA soldiers who wanted to recruit them. It ended in a bloodbath, but with his new abilities, he escaped the country. It took him awhile to get there, but eventually he made his way to Toronto as an immigrant, working humble jobs. He didn't really have any friends, his family was gone, and he was in a new country he wasn't familiar with. It was a rough time for him.<br /> <br /> Then the Family enters into the picture. They're a family of wolf-blooded and uratha with a few humans that are both an actual family and a pack. They take him into the pack, teach him about Uratha society and 'adopt him' in a manner of speaking. Finding comfort in the strong cultural identity of the Forsaken, he really takes to Purity as his favored renown, and he tries his best to prove himself worthy of being part of this new family.<br /> <br /> Already, he's setting down roots. He has a relationship with one of the wolf-blooded in the family, Celia, and he is close with the newest members of the Family to undergo the First Change. He thinks a lot about the future, something he's had a hard time doing before, and he finds himself worrying. Would he be a good enough father? Would he be a good enough Wolf? Does the Family truly accept him? It's a constant source of doubt in his mind.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> The theme of the game I'm intending to play him in is about the interplay of family, and I thought it might be interesting to explore it from an outside perspective. Santino is a guy who hasn't had a family in a really long time, has endured an unimaginable amount of loss in his life, so he is desperate to protect his newfound family, whatever flaws it might have. He really wants to be a part of it, but he recognizes he's also very alien to them, and it's a source of pain and frustration for him.<br /> <br /> Another theme we've discussed is a critical look at Uratha as a warrior-culture and society. The Family brought Santino in and taught him the party line as it were, encouraging him to Hunt, not just because he needs to, but because it is good, the right thing to do. But Santino is one of the Lost Boys, a man who has undergone considerable trauma being made the pawn of others in war, experienced great suffering via violence and these other things. How does that complicate the Uratha existence and modus operandi? What does the Family do by taking him in, and are they doing the right thing by putting him in this world of violence? Does he have a choice in the matter?<br /> <br /> These are questions I'm definitely interested in exploring with him. Do you guys have any thoughts or comments? I'd love to hear them! I am also very keen on discussing your concepts as well. What kinds of characters do you have on the brain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:53:55-07:00","id":863997,"title":"","content":"My Werewolf character, already played.<br /> \u200bFaith Grissholm, privileged daughter of an upper class family (extended family) with a proud history of Naval service. She had planned out her whole future, good grades in high school, join the Navy and attend the academy with possibly one day the command of her own ship (dream big). After spending her youth sacrificing and working towards this future she undergoes first change (1ed). Now she learns that her family is part of a wolf blooded clan and with the change came a whole new plan, one designed by the clan patriarch, hers is now scrap. They even told her who she would marry (or at least have children with). She rebels, symbolically runs away by joining an unrelated pack (the players') and after a life of following the straight and narrow becomes a little bit of the &quot;I'll try anything once&quot; sort of wild child. The patriarch hasn't given up on her though, he figures one way or another she will still serve the clan's purposes, or her children will.<br /> I wanted to explore the wolf blooded/Uratha connection and play with the total life disruption of the change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T18:16:49-07:00","id":864013,"title":"","content":"Played and loved him to bits, but:<br /> <br /> Lionheart (real name Richard Brandt) was a police officer and happily married man when the Fae stole him away to fight endlessly in a petty war for their amusement. After seeing too much horror and bloodshed, he organized a suicidal attack with all the other changelings of the domain... only to run from battle and escape while his companions were slaughtered. Returned to reality, he scorns his wife, children, and fetch, in favor of rising to prominence in the local Summer Court; his eventual goal is to forge the freehold into an army that can march back into Arcadia and kill his former Keeper, but he understands and anticipates that it's likely a doomed effort. Pride and survivor's guilt conspire against him, constantly working towards his self-destruction.<br /> <br /> It was really fun to play a charismatic, popular figure in the local political structure who rose to hated tyranny and was eventually killed by the other player characters on the eve of battle with one of the Gentry; they voted to dissolve the freehold rather than likely be wiped out in the fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:42:27-07:00","id":864055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=864013#post864013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Played and loved him to bits, but:<br /> <br /> Lionheart (real name Richard Brandt) was a police officer and happily married man when the Fae stole him away to fight endlessly in a petty war for their amusement. After seeing too much horror and bloodshed, he organized a suicidal attack with all the other changelings of the domain... only to run from battle and escape while his companions were slaughtered. Returned to reality, he scorns his wife, children, and fetch, in favor of rising to prominence in the local Summer Court; his eventual goal is to forge the freehold into an army that can march back into Arcadia and kill his former Keeper, but he understands and anticipates that it's likely a doomed effort. Pride and survivor's guilt conspire against him, constantly working towards his self-destruction.<br /> <br /> It was really fun to play a charismatic, popular figure in the local political structure who rose to hated tyranny and was eventually killed by the other player characters on the eve of battle with one of the Gentry; they voted to dissolve the freehold rather than likely be wiped out in the fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>He sounds very evocative of a lot of soldier archetypes, cool! <br /> <br /> Did your ST plan for it to go that way, or did it just sort of happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:06:35-07:00","id":864067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=864055#post864055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He sounds very evocative of a lot of soldier archetypes, cool! <br /> <br /> Did your ST plan for it to go that way, or did it just sort of happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was coming at the core PTSD metaphor of Changeling from a military perspective, which is the closest I can understand it through personally (my dad's a vet and I grew up working at an aerospace museum in a military town). More simply than that, I wanted to play the Cowardly Lion by way of Scar from The Lion King, and then drag that character as far along a path of bullshit justified by an increasingly thin &quot;for the greater good&quot; as he spiraled ever closer to a suicidal blaze of glory.<br /> <br /> I literally enjoyed playing Lionheart so much that I don't want to play Changeling again, because he hit everything I love about the game and its themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:45:37-07:00","id":864111,"title":"","content":"Leetsepeak, I like Santino Duku. The fact you didn't take the Sacred Hunt for granted is admirable, and a totally valid way to play the game.<br /> <br /> I've been trying to round out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823666#post823666\"><b>a Namtaru Collector.</b></a> His Horror would be <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824480#post824480\"><b>like this.</b></a> I'm having a hard time imagining how exactly he would Feed, but I know he would be mainly Low Satiety.<br /> <br /> I considered making him a sort of Franken Fran figure. That is, he almost always has a remedy or surgery of his own design that can fix problems big and small...but do you really need the help of such a shady character? Can't you figure this out on your own? He does his best to minimize side-effects, but he can't guarantee you'll walk out of his Lair just fine if you don't give him all the information about your condition that he needs, which can be a lot. And if he thinks you can give him more than just cash, he might offer...freebies. He tells himself he always puts all the cards on the table, but his Hunger sometimes growls louder than his remaining conventional morality.<br /> <br /> So, he could be Namtaru as Fear Of The Cure, the uncertainty of easy solutions. What sort of Aspirations would go well with all of that? I imagine that when it comes to Prometheans and Changelings, he can be anything from an open-minded and highly useful mentor, to a Qashmal/True Fae coming to cull the weak and gullible with plagues disguised as panacea.<br /> <br /> EDIT: By the way, he didn't really build the house/laboratory in his Lair. He grew it. Sometimes, when you're lying down on a surprisingly comfortable operating table, surrounded by the impeccable, fractal blades, you can hear the Lair. You just can't tell if that's a vast pulse, or humming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-12-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:26:30-07:00","id":864258,"title":"","content":"Not much of a concept, but here's a Beast idea inspired by a post on this thread's &quot;Silly&quot; counterpart. Basically the idea is to play with the idea of the &quot;Last Girl&quot;, the sole survivor of the slasher movie. More specifically, she survived because she underwent her Devouring/Homecoming after the last of her friends died, and then proceeded to show the killer what <b>true</b> terror looks like. Haven't figured out more than that, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:47:04-07:00","id":864446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=864258#post864258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much of a concept, but here's a Beast idea inspired by a post on this thread's &quot;Silly&quot; counterpart. Basically the idea is to play with the idea of the &quot;Last Girl&quot;, the sole survivor of the slasher movie. More specifically, she survived because she underwent her Devouring/Homecoming after the last of her friends died, and then proceeded to show the killer what <b>true</b> terror looks like. Haven't figured out more than that, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;That little girl from ever Horror Film ever&quot; An Apex Beast at the age of 16. Has been a beast since about 8 years old, no family left living. Feeds her Hunger by &quot;Arranging&quot; for a mad serial Killer to appear and Feeds on the terror of those trying to Protect her (Relies on the Big Brother/Sister Instinct to get people to &quot;Protect&quot; her while Baiting the people into blatant traps and bad ideas) Has Nightmares that make people do the Wrong thing in situations that should really be clear cut on what they should do.<br /> Her Horror is a Massive Spider entity-thing that loves... I mean.... Looovvvvvveeeeesss to make people into puppets for her amusements. (For extra sympathy... She might have Disassociative Identity Disorder and thinks the Horror is something seperate from her, For added Creep... She ACTS like she has DID, but in fact doesn't and Loves using that to trap More people in her Web.)<br /> <br /> This one?<br /> <br /> And Thanks for liking it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:48:22-07:00","id":864450,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T15:56:43-07:00","id":865167,"title":"","content":"Right, sorry for the second post. <br /> <br /> Another idea I've had is a character for the Sundered World Dark Era. I'm not a backer, so I'm working from what I've picked up; forgive me if I get anything wrong. Gonna put this in spoilers, since I've put more thought into this than someone who doesn't actually have the document in question has any right to.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He's a Mage (or Wise, as the case may be), to be specific, a Obrimos (or Storm-Wise). Considering that the People apparently go with title names, I'm think of calling him... well, <i>Something</i> of Names; currently I'm considering Carver of Names, Assessor of Names, or Seeker of Names, but I'm not really sure. I'm not sure what the Vinca people looked like, but I imagine him as being tall and somewhat thin, the sort of person who's always moving, pointing, gesturing, and fidgeting whenever, constantly filled with energy. <br /> <br /> As for his personality, he's an energetic soul, filled to the brim with an obsessive curiosity. He talks quickly and almost breathlessly, barraging the poor souls who interacts with him with questions, suggestions, and queries. For him, everything is fascinating, everything is worthy of total understanding. Even a simple bull can inspire a involved study as to its nature. But the biggest question, in the end, is &quot;How can this help the People?&quot; For he believes in the ascendancy of humanity, the belief it is the right of the people in particular and mankind in general have the natural right to tame the chaos of the world into a newer, better order. To this end he encourages cooperation and alliance between villages, people, and even potentially peoples. When he allows himself to dream really big, he dreams of all of humanity (possibly even the wolf-shifters and their ilk, if they can learn to be civilized) united into one grand village, a towering wonder that rivals any ruin of the time before, surrounded by farmland as far as the eye can see, a world of peace and plenty where humanity has tamed all of existence. <br /> <br /> Mechanically, I'm thinking he favors Mental and Social Attributes and Skills. I'm thinking going for the Virtuous Merit, if I can. In regards to the Arcana, well, the most <i>practical</i> would probably be Forces (storms and flame), Life (Agriculture and wild animals), and Spirit (because those are a big threat in these days), while the Arcana most useful to his ambitions seem to be Prime (to know and use the Forms and Names of a thing), Mind (better understand and navigate the Astral), and Space (travel and communication at a distance). To be honest, I imagine he would like to get a dot in all the Arcana (foe access to the Knowing, Unveiling, and Mage Sight), but that sounds impractical. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T16:12:59-07:00","id":865174,"title":"","content":"I could use some help with a character concept; which Path would be best for a Mage focused on reincarnation? <br /> <br /> Unrelated to that, I'm waiting for the Dark Eras Companion to give me guidance for a Mage obsessed with the mysteries of Irem. I'm really liking the idea of going for Acanthus, because of how Fate is interestingly wrapped up with the Arisen and the Time parallels between the Time Before and the Rite of Return are super interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T16:20:00-07:00","id":865176,"title":"","content":"Acanthus and Moros are the most &quot;go-to&quot; Paths for Reincarnation thingies. Probably Acanthus with Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T16:37:17-07:00","id":865185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865176#post865176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acanthus and Moros are the most &amp;quot;go-to&amp;quot; Paths for Reincarnation thingies. Probably Acanthus with Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw a pretty compelling argument for Mind working with past lives via the Astral somewhere, finding the memories of past lives in the deepest corners of the Oneiros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T17:31:21-07:00","id":865214,"title":"","content":"I could see a really nice Left Handed Legacy Villain out of this; someone who goes and canibalizes memories they think are theirs, in order to become &quot;complete&quot;, and going bonkers in the process due to their mind becoming an insane patchjob of unrelated memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:34:58-07:00","id":865274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865174#post865174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could use some help with a character concept; which Path would be best for a Mage focused on reincarnation?<br /> <br /> Unrelated to that, I'm waiting for the Dark Eras Companion to give me guidance for a Mage obsessed with the mysteries of Irem. I'm really liking the idea of going for Acanthus, because of how Fate is interestingly wrapped up with the Arisen and the Time parallels between the Time Before and the Rite of Return are super interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div> What kind of reincarnation are we talking about? I can try to help you round out this concept. Could you please help me do the same for my Namtaru Collector mentioned above? I don't know enough about Mummy to help with the second concept, sorry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:40:39-07:00","id":865277,"title":"","content":"Well, if we are also asking character advice here, I've been stalled trying to come up with a good &quot;Mummy-Detective&quot; character. They'd be really interested in all kinds of mysteries (though their cult would handle most of the ground work). I was trying to decide on Decree and Guild. I can see Sheut, for the Noir feel, or Ka, for the determination to follow through, or Ren, for the intellectual focus. Maa-Kep for the helpful, secret finder, or Sesha Hebsu, for the legal focus and judge-y feel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:13:27-07:00","id":865291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865174#post865174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could use some help with a character concept; which Path would be best for a Mage focused on reincarnation?<br /> <br /> Unrelated to that, I'm waiting for the Dark Eras Companion to give me guidance for a Mage obsessed with the mysteries of Irem. I'm really liking the idea of going for Acanthus, because of how Fate is interestingly wrapped up with the Arisen and the Time parallels between the Time Before and the Rite of Return are super interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, while I think Moros could do this, I think this would be an excellent purview of an Acanthus Legacy with Mind, people who can use the Astral or something within it to go to the past within the Astral. Maybe they find Oneiroi that are somehow linked to their own (and perhaps interpret this as reincarnation?) and then travel back in time to when that person was alive, and engage in some kind of shadow play of their memories within the Astral. <br /> <br /> Since I know you've cited Assassin's Creed as one of your interests in exploring this concept, that could serve to recreate the concept of these characters experiencing what their forebears did. It could also reveal real information, but I have to double check what happens to your Oneiros when you die. Does Astral Realm discuss this at all?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:37:01-07:00","id":865298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865277#post865277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if we are also asking character advice here, I've been stalled trying to come up with a good &quot;Mummy-Detective&quot; character. They'd be really interested in all kinds of mysteries (though their cult would handle most of the ground work). I was trying to decide on Decree and Guild. I can see Sheut, for the Noir feel, or Ka, for the determination to follow through, or Ren, for the intellectual focus. Maa-Kep for the helpful, secret finder, or Sesha Hebsu, for the legal focus and judge-y feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>The go-to for characters obsessed with secrets and mysteries is the Decree of Ren/Name, also known as the Serpent-Headed; they seek to understand the &quot;names&quot; and true natures of all things, to the point of obsession. As for the detective side of things, it's a toss up between the Maa-Kep (if your character is big on the human element) or the Sesha-Hebsu (for the academic and occult side of things). The Judge Bastu governs those who have tried to cheat justice, which is pretty great for a detective's patron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-14-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:49:45-07:00","id":865302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865277#post865277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if we are also asking character advice here, I've been stalled trying to come up with a good &quot;Mummy-Detective&quot; character. They'd be really interested in all kinds of mysteries (though their cult would handle most of the ground work). I was trying to decide on Decree and Guild. I can see Sheut, for the Noir feel, or Ka, for the determination to follow through, or Ren, for the intellectual focus. Maa-Kep for the helpful, secret finder, or Sesha Hebsu, for the legal focus and judge-y feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely feeling Sesha Hebsu. Think about the bureaucrat that makes sure the books are clean and that nobody is misusing company resources, and I think you can come up with an interesting Inquirer type of character. They like keeping records of stuff, and somebody has to keep records of mysteries and how they were solved!<br /> <br /> I don't know enough about the Pillars, but I'd definitely shoot for a Judge who has a thing about keeping secrets from important people or somesuch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:43:30-07:00","id":865394,"title":"","content":"Well this is one I've done before in Witchcraft... But I'd like to try it in CofD sometime.<br /> <br /> Ashley &quot;Ash&quot; Henry's is a serial Immortal, Cursed to live in interesting times and Die before the age of 40. Always to Die Horribly, Never happily (And all those he cares for will also be killed off to so he can suffer with them for a period in a Hell-world before his rebirth). Over the lives he has learned afew tricks, Like biokinetics/telekinetics and self healing, He has been a Vampire, a Crusader, a Hunter and a mage... but his soul always returns to its baseline form once he &quot;Dies&quot; (Becoming a Vampire generally doesn't count in that sense because he still.. &quot;Lives&quot; and it makes him suffer more.)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a Blue-book Immortal with some powers from Second Sight.. but advice is always appreciated. (Plus i still need to find a game to let me play it.. so I've got time)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T04:46:18-07:00","id":865420,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking of a Mummy (probably Deceived) called Khufhu of the Thousand Faces, an actor back in Irem who has a history of imitating already worshiped figures or beings related to such figures (The Second Coming of Christ, the Son of Muhammad, an Avatar of Vishnu, etc.) in order to build up worshipers from already existing stock, until, while impersonating one of the Loa, he found himself coming to respect and even believe in the sevite religion, adapting and fitting it in to Iremite religious practices.<br /> <br /> Also a Maa-Kep called Amset, Child of the Wandering Star, who mostly exists because I want to figure out a way to get the gunslinger archetype to work with the fact that a lot of enemies in Mummy, including other Mummies, are really tough to kill with an actual firearm. Currently, I'm thinking flare guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:54:38-07:00","id":865479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865420#post865420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a Maa-Kep called Amset, Child of the Wandering Star, who mostly exists because I want to figure out a way to get the gunslinger archetype to work with the fact that a lot of enemies in Mummy, including other Mummies, are really tough to kill with an actual firearm. Currently, I'm thinking flare guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incendiary ammunition. Alternatively, a Relic firearm should do the trick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T10:51:08-07:00","id":865596,"title":"","content":"I have a few characters who I played in sadly short lived games that I'd quite like to play in a longer campaign. Formost among them is a Changeling with the personality, skills and ambitions of a typical evil sorceress along the lines of Snow White's evil stepmother who presents herself to the world as a perpetually distressed damsel. In 2E parlance she'd be a Grimm Damsel - hence why I keep asking David for a Damsel Kith.<br /> <br /> The most recent idea to pop into my head was a Beast Ugallu Tyrant who takes the form of an evil cheerleader with a giant bee hive queen shaped horror. Her lesson is that you have to fit in and be normal to survive in life, which she teaches with great cruelty to her classmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T13:14:30-07:00","id":865666,"title":"","content":"I had a Changeling who was a Gristlegrinder Fairest; she was taken to Arcadia to be a classic &quot;princess in the tower,&quot; but she devoured all of the fair knights sent to save her and escaped herself. Wanted to explore anorexia within a roleplaying context and also enjoy being a scrawny Winter waif who could hold her own in a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:26:16-07:00","id":865744,"title":"","content":"Ow a Concept i've wanted to play for quite a while.... &quot;Conceptional Thief&quot; someone who Steals Concepts and important objects for everyone/thing. Like... someone's Time, Health, Knowledge. He has no use for it... just that he takes it. (Borrowed the Concept from King of Bandit Jing.. the Anime. The Manga is abit more.. Well, Explained.) At first he takes objects that symbolize the thing he's stealing.. later its just the Thing, no symbolic object needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T09:47:56-07:00","id":866424,"title":"","content":"A demon who before he fell was a 'repair man' and though he fixed what was broken he never created anything himself. That paired with how much he had to repair a so called perfect being is why he fell (with the possibility that the fall was planned). He misses being able to look at something and simply understanding everything about what he is looking at and is striving to reach that state again. What he dreams beyond all else is to be able to build infrastructure himself and he will use any method he can to achieve these results. Maybe once he does he can destroy the machine and put something truly perfect in its place but for now he just has to gather knowledge.<br /> <br /> The truth of the matter is there is a reason he never created anything as an angel. He was not a wheel but one of the machine's eyes who inspected how flaws could be repaired. So what drives him the most is a misinterpretation of his old purpose.<br /> <br /> Analyst Interrogator (and later also saboteur)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T12:12:39-07:00","id":866482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865277#post865277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if we are also asking character advice here, I've been stalled trying to come up with a good &amp;quot;Mummy-Detective&amp;quot; character. They'd be really interested in all kinds of mysteries (though their cult would handle most of the ground work). I was trying to decide on Decree and Guild. I can see Sheut, for the Noir feel, or Ka, for the determination to follow through, or Ren, for the intellectual focus. Maa-Kep for the helpful, secret finder, or Sesha Hebsu, for the legal focus and judge-y feel?</div> </div> </div> </div> That sounds a bit like Will Eisner's <b><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">The Spirit</a></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:19:13-07:00","id":866522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=866482#post866482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That sounds a bit like Will Eisner's <b><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">The Spirit</a></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bWell, with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> 's advice, he's (in rough concept form) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:45:50-07:00","id":866567,"title":"","content":"Some Demon ideas.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;Mr. Powers&quot;- Not sure what Incarnation, but I imagine him as a Inquisitor-Tempter. Whatever he is, his core concept is based around Show of Power and the fact that there ain't no rule that says you can't give Supernatural Merits with a Pact. I imagine him as a sort of &quot;power broker&quot;, giving out innate ability and magic items (Show of Power Gadgets) both to gain temporal power and because he believes he can find the secret to his own transcendence by studying how humans become something more and less than they once were.<br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;Mr. Mind&quot;- An Analyst Saboteur/Inquisitor, he was originally created to assess the Machine's operation in the region of the game and determine what the optimal course might be. Instead, he determined that the suffering it caused meant that the most correct option would be to remove its influence. Since he's not exactly a bruiser, he mostly accomplishes this by planing and analyzing for others. He would be interested in allying with/suborning any Hunters or Brothers of the Machine Gun in the area. His starting Key would be Imagine, obviously. <br /> <br /> \u2022&quot;Director Thorn&quot;- Inspired by one of the sample Interlocks in the Storyteller's Guide, Thorn is a Psychopomp Tempter. Originally assigned to the administrative portion of a construction company to aid with the creation of Infrastructure during a period of high expansion for the Machine, he became obsessed with a Hedge gate he found on one of the properties, to the point he neglected his duties and Fell. His goal is to &quot;domesticate&quot; the Hedge, forming an unassailable fortress within and utilizing its resources to his advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T00:06:49-07:00","id":866701,"title":"","content":"I've got one that strains canon somewhat, but I like the idea of a very fresh Pentacle mage (likely still an apprentice) that somehow receives visions from one of the Exarchs. She doesn't know it as such, and isn't being commanded to do anything malevolent, but is very confused by and interested in the god that seems to have chosen her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-17-2016, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T05:00:48-07:00","id":866756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=866701#post866701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got one that strains canon somewhat, but I like the idea of a very fresh Pentacle mage (likely still an apprentice) that somehow receives visions from one of the Exarchs. She doesn't know it as such, and isn't being commanded to do anything malevolent, but is very confused by and interested in the god that seems to have chosen her.</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe that Signs of Sorcery will include a section on Pentacle Mages and calling on the Exarchs, so maybe you might be able to find inspiration when that comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T17:01:43-07:00","id":870762,"title":"","content":"Oh I just remembered one:<br /> <br /> A Hunter version of Sam Haight - someone who's, through aliases, being a double or triple agent, or just plain lies and graft, been a member of all the Conspiracies and has their Endowments. They hate him as a security risk (and thief), but the street-level Cells he helps out love him.<br /> <br /> For added fun, combine with a Steven Heck personality and/or multiple choice past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T01:40:25-07:00","id":871054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=870762#post870762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I just remembered one:<br /> <br /> A Hunter version of Sam Haight - someone who's, through aliases, being a double or triple agent, or just plain lies and graft, been a member of all the Conspiracies and has their Endowments. They hate him as a security risk (and thief), but the street-level Cells he helps out love him.<br /> <br /> For added fun, combine with a Steven Heck personality and/or multiple choice past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would he also have all the minor templates possible to not be born into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T04:32:05-07:00","id":871105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=871054#post871054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would he also have all the minor templates possible to not be born into?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No? The purpose was more &quot;Hey, Endowments are accessible to anybody that is a part of the Conspiracy. What if someone changes Conspiracy? They might have some supply issues with some, but they'd keep the Endowments...&quot; extrapolated to<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/instances2/500x/5421036.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So yeah, he picks up a few Advance Armory supplies that have &quot;fallen off the truck&quot;, brews a few Elixirs, has had some surgery done, polishes his small collection of Relics, says the odd mumbled prayer from time to time (potentially after invoking the power of the Pit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-22-2016, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:37:06-07:00","id":871442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=871105#post871105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No? The purpose was more &quot;Hey, Endowments are accessible to anybody that is a part of the Conspiracy. What if someone changes Conspiracy? They might have some supply issues with some, but they'd keep the Endowments...&quot; .</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant it more as a &quot;If we're doing Sam Haight expy-thing, we might as well go all-out&quot; type of joke. I understand what you meant perfectly, and have in fact toyed around with a similiar concept in one of my games. In practice though it did not work out that well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:37:38-07:00","id":871535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=871442#post871442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant it more as a &quot;If we're doing Sam Haight expy-thing, we might as well go all-out&quot; type of joke. I understand what you meant perfectly, and have in fact toyed around with a similiar concept in one of my games. In practice though it did not work out that well</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, what went wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:41:41-07:00","id":871617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=871535#post871535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, what went wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it was just the fault of bad STing or else, but the power difference between said multiple-endowed player and the rest of the party was comparable to having an archmaster in a party of regular mages.<br /> Okay, maybe not that much... Maybe like having an Adept in a party of freshly Awakened would be a better comparision? Probably. Either way, there was a visible power level difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:53:06-07:00","id":871630,"title":"","content":"I have an Arisen waiting for an eventual chronicle to roll around; Nakhte (of the many titles, because that's the fun part of being a semi-mythical demigod). In life, he was the chief of a barbarian tribe conquered by Irem. Impressed by his tenacity and strength, they allowed him to live if he converted to the worship of the Judges and he became a zealot for the Su-Menent, earning the Rite of Return. His Cults have varied across the ages, but are almost always pulled from the ranks of soldiers (Medjay mercenaries during the First Turn, crippled former legionaries during the time of Rome, heretical crusaders, the SAS troops who stopped the Nazis from getting him, etc). He's definitely a kind of warrior-poet, always traveling, with his fire and rage tempered by a harsh understanding of how much he's lost and forgotten.<br /> <br /> With him comes a pre-made antagonist. Nakhte was allowed to convert and serve gloriously, but his entire tribe was enslaved and then sacrificed to the Devourer; many of them have hunted him across the ages for his &quot;treachery,&quot; which he doesn't remember whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T14:22:19-07:00","id":871729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=871617#post871617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if it was just the fault of bad STing or else, but the power difference between said multiple-endowed player and the rest of the party was comparable to having an archmaster in a party of regular mages.<br /> Okay, maybe not that much... Maybe like having an Adept in a party of freshly Awakened would be a better comparision? Probably. Either way, there was a visible power level difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was intending the character to be an NPC (used when making formerly insurmountable challenges merely difficult). I can see how them in a normal Hunter Cell would be pretty overpowered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=871630#post871630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an Arisen waiting for an eventual chronicle to roll around; Nakhte (of the many titles, because that's the fun part of being a semi-mythical demigod).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is one of his titles &quot;Of The Many Titles&quot;? :-P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=871630#post871630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With him comes a pre-made antagonist. Nakhte was allowed to convert and serve gloriously, but his entire tribe was enslaved and then sacrificed to the Devourer; many of them have hunted him across the ages for his &quot;treachery,&quot; which he doesn't remember whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I love those for older, forgetful characters. So easy for hooks. I think the most amusing instance I saw was in a very long lived Possessed who was finally confronted by a nemesis who was plaguing them for over 200 years. It pretty much boiled down to &quot;But for me, it was Tuesday&quot; which pissed said self-appointed nemesis off even further. Good times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-22-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T16:05:45-07:00","id":871844,"title":"","content":"I had a random thought of the victim of a Fey abduction who escapes by awakening, a new Mage who is permanently enscrolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T12:08:30-07:00","id":873928,"title":"","content":"An B:tP idea I had thanks to some chatter on the Player's Guide thread is a Beast-Hunter; that is, a character that hunts Beasts while also being a Beast. To clarify, they're a Nemesis (not sure about Family) who feeds by seeking out those children of the Dark Mother (with a focus on the Begotten but also dealing with other supernaturals) who &quot;feed&quot; in ways that threaten the Masquerade or cause undue harm to normal people and (non-lethally) cracking skulls until they get the message. The character does this both out of concern for the mortals in the area and because they worry that being too blatantly predatory could render the local population less &quot;sustainable&quot; as a resource, not to mention provoking Hunters or Heroes. They likely see themselves as fulfilling a necessary duty, while others may well see them as a busybody or a traitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:27:40-07:00","id":874024,"title":"","content":"I'm not conversant with Beast, but considering how their Nightmares are subtle (as in, no pyrotechnics), their focus on &quot;teamwork/family&quot;, and their Lair, I wonder how a Begotten Crime Boss would play out. Police trying to raid you? Have fun storming the Lair. Need to smuggle things? Primordial Pathways. Underlings getting uppity? Show them what Fear is (and get a meal out of it too). And just think of all the fun lieutenants you could have...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T15:05:35-07:00","id":874048,"title":"","content":"An idea I've had for a Demon character is an Analyst or Psychopomp Tempter embeded (pun not intended) in Utopia Now. Basically, they were created to work within the group (to watch them to see if they ever become truely dangerous if an Analyst, and to aid in proper identification and disposal of damaged/useless Infrastructure if Psychopomp), and now that they've Fell they hope to utilize the group's goals and methods to both aquire power and build a proper Hell. One idea I like for characterization is that the Unchained's Fall instilled them with a strong sense of compassion, which means that, while they're still part of the group, they find some of the conpany's philosophy rather abhorent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:32:47-07:00","id":874341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874024#post874024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not conversant with Beast, but considering how their Nightmares are subtle (as in, no pyrotechnics), their focus on &quot;teamwork/family&quot;, and their Lair, I wonder how a Begotten Crime Boss would play out. Police trying to raid you? Have fun storming the Lair. Need to smuggle things? Primordial Pathways. Underlings getting uppity? Show them what Fear is (and get a meal out of it too). And just think of all the fun lieutenants you could have...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had an idea for a campaign centered on a crime family that is composed of Beasts, in which the various characters fulfill different roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:43:24-07:00","id":874442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865596#post865596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few characters who I played in sadly short lived games that I'd quite like to play in a longer campaign. Formost among them is a Changeling with the personality, skills and ambitions of a typical evil sorceress along the lines of Snow White's evil stepmother who presents herself to the world as a perpetually distressed damsel. In 2E parlance she'd be a Grimm Damsel - hence why I keep asking David for a Damsel Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. There happens to be a Damsel kith brewed up in my Homebrew kith thread. Feel free to give it a look and see if it works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:45:34-07:00","id":874444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874341#post874341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've had an idea for a campaign centered on a crime family that is composed of Beasts, in which the various characters fulfill different roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to assume they're all different Families as well as Hungers. But yeah, that said, I can see your stuff for Totemic Beasts and Primordial Sorcerers fitting well with that concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:51:14-07:00","id":874452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=865394#post865394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this is one I've done before in Witchcraft... But I'd like to try it in CofD sometime.<br /> <br /> Ashley &amp;quot;Ash&amp;quot; Henry's is a serial Immortal, Cursed to live in interesting times and Die before the age of 40. Always to Die Horribly, Never happily (And all those he cares for will also be killed off to so he can suffer with them for a period in a Hell-world before his rebirth). Over the lives he has learned afew tricks, Like biokinetics/telekinetics and self healing, He has been a Vampire, a Crusader, a Hunter and a mage... but his soul always returns to its baseline form once he &amp;quot;Dies&amp;quot; (Becoming a Vampire generally doesn't count in that sense because he still.. &amp;quot;Lives&amp;quot; and it makes him suffer more.)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a Blue-book Immortal with some powers from Second Sight.. but advice is always appreciated. (Plus i still need to find a game to let me play it.. so I've got time)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually started working out on 2E conversions for Immortals. That said, your character clearly is one of the Reborn, just like another Immortal I have thought up.<br /> <br /> Moving on. I was thinking that as a minor template, Reborn could begin play with the following Merits...<br /> <br /> * Eidetic Memory (plus its Advanced version?)<br /> * Meditative Mind (one dot, or already at four?)<br /> <br /> That's all I got, so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:04:18-07:00","id":874542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874452#post874452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually started working out on 2E conversions for Immortals. That said, your character clearly is one of the Reborn, just like another Immortal I have thought up.<br /> <br /> Moving on. I was thinking that as a minor template, Reborn could begin play with the following Merits...<br /> <br /> * Eidetic Memory (plus its Advanced version?)<br /> * Meditative Mind (one dot, or already at four?)<br /> <br /> That's all I got, so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think they need those before they even become Reborn. But that makes it kinda moot, from a character generation standpoint.<br /> <br /> Aside: I've always found ancient characters hard to justify as new-character-comparable in a modern game. They <i>should</i> have bucket loads of XP and development throughout the years. Something I've thought about doing was having them with a &quot;true&quot; advanced character sheet, and their current one, and offering big discounts (XP and Beat rebates) towards reaching their &quot;old&quot; skills/Merits/etc., when applicable (on account of, they are just retraining, rather than acquiring to begin with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-26-2016, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:28:45-07:00","id":874559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874542#post874542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd think they need those before they even become Reborn. But that makes it kinda moot, from a character generation standpoint.<br /> <br /> Aside: I've always found ancient characters hard to justify as new-character-comparable in a modern game. They <i>should</i> have bucket loads of XP and development throughout the years. Something I've thought about doing was having them with a &quot;true&quot; advanced character sheet, and their current one, and offering big discounts (XP and Beat rebates) towards reaching their &quot;old&quot; skills/Merits/etc., when applicable (on account of, they are just retraining, rather than acquiring to begin with).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Newly reborn Immortal (Atleast new to this Incarnation) I'd justify it as allowing them to Purchase most of the Merits/Endowments that is in the Character Previous lifetimes... (In practice only afew are likely to be interesting enough to allow skills/tricks etc.) Essentially I'd make the Initial merit Scaled/Rated based on Previous Lifetimes (Say 1 rank is 2-3, 2 ranks are 4-6, up to 5 being something like 20+ previous lives. Not every lifetime is important... So... Each rank allows a set of Endowments/skills to be purchased without &quot;Reason/Training&quot; the justification being... You know them from before it's just taken a while to make them viable for &quot;Modern&quot; life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:47:02-07:00","id":874845,"title":"","content":"Another idea I've had; a Hero (from Beast: the Primordial) who ends up undergoing a change into one of the Major Templates, only for the resultant metaphysical and psychological shifts to cure him of his madness. He's understandably somewhat horrified of what he was and did, especially since he lacks an understanding of what Heroes and Beasts actually are. For some reason I'm leaning towards Mage, but anything a normal human can turn into (except probably Beast) would fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:50:40-07:00","id":874847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874845#post874845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea I've had; a Hero (from Beast: the Primordial) who ends up undergoing a change into one of the Major Templates, only for the resultant metaphysical and psychological shifts to cure him of his madness. He's understandably somewhat horrified of what he was and did, especially since he lacks an understanding of what Heroes and Beasts actually are. For some reason I'm leaning towards Mage, but anything a normal human can turn into (except probably Beast) would fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eater? Deviant? Changeling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:15:53-07:00","id":874868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874559#post874559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a Newly reborn Immortal (Atleast new to this Incarnation) I'd justify it as allowing them to Purchase most of the Merits/Endowments that is in the Character Previous lifetimes... (In practice only afew are likely to be interesting enough to allow skills/tricks etc.) Essentially I'd make the Initial merit Scaled/Rated based on Previous Lifetimes (Say 1 rank is 2-3, 2 ranks are 4-6, up to 5 being something like 20+ previous lives. Not every lifetime is important... So... Each rank allows a set of Endowments/skills to be purchased without &amp;quot;Reason/Training&amp;quot; the justification being... You know them from before it's just taken a while to make them viable for &amp;quot;Modern&amp;quot; life.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually works. Especially if you take Hawkgirl and Hawkman from the Arrowverse as an example for (natural) Reborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:21:04-07:00","id":874876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874847#post874847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sin-Eater? Deviant? Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. Sin-Eater Ex-Hero would probably have died due to a mistake while hunting, accepting the Bargain with the hope of becoming an even greater slayer... only, upon fully awakening, to wonder &quot;What the <i>heck</i> am I doing with my life?&quot;, as all their excuses and justifications seem as hollow and dead as the thing tethered to his soul. <br /> <br /> The Changeling Ex-Hero would probably be more gradual. Maybe his Keeper thrust him into a fantasy world to slay monsters as a knight, or maybe he was kept as pride in the Keeper's hell-gallery, but either way elation or rage slowly ferment into genuine contemplation, which causes him to look back and realize how foolish he was. Thanks to his changed mindset, his Keeper's snares become meaningless, allowing his escape. Seeming-wise I'm think Fairest (because only be accepting he wasn't the knight in shining armor already could he actually become it) or Elemental (to represent his detachment from his ego, in comparison to his old self).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:35:55-07:00","id":874895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=874876#post874876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changeling Ex-Hero would probably be more gradual. Maybe his Keeper thrust him into a fantasy world to slay monsters as a knight, or maybe he was kept as pride in the Keeper's hell-gallery, but either way elation or rage slowly ferment into genuine contemplation, which causes him to look back and realize how foolish he was. Thanks to his changed mindset, his Keeper's snares become meaningless, allowing his escape. Seeming-wise I'm think Fairest (because only be accepting he wasn't the knight in shining armor already could he actually become it) or Elemental (to represent his detachment from his ego, in comparison to his old self).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could also see Darkling, born of the realization that the &quot;monster&quot; he was sent to fight was another (former) human like them... and they killed/betrayed them anyways to escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T17:40:54-07:00","id":875041,"title":"","content":"This one is vague in my head right now, but here goes. An old and powerful Beast (maybe even an Incarnate) that enters the mortal realm once every [insert mythical cycle here], when the proper ritual is performed or just when something unusual catches their attention. Their Brood consists of those monsters that even other monsters fear: Centimani, Scelesti, Bale Hounds and so on. Whether they do this out of sympathy, a sick sense of humor, too much curiosity or something else is unknown, and if asked, they tell a different story every time.<br /> <br /> They would be a major antagonist who takes in those other NPCs that the players wronged somehow or thought were defeated. Their Family is probably Namtaru (for consorting with scum and loving it) or Ugallu (for always knowing when someone has the potential to become a true monster). I'm not sure what their Hunger(s) would be, but they would probably favor High Satiety through Hunger Management 3, lots of Family Dinners and Feedings that are theatrical, bizarre and gruesome.<br /> <br /> As for their personality, I don't think they would have a tragic past that motivates them or anything like that. They'd be more like Bill Cipher from Gravity Falls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-26-2016, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T18:23:51-07:00","id":875087,"title":"","content":"I'm currently having a weird urge to make my first 2nd ED Mage character a classical genius newbie - a character who awakened week ago, but has Gnosis 2 (goodbye, 5 merit dots), no Order membership and literally learns the setting as we go in. <br /> I usually play characters with deep understanding of the settings (because I'm probably the most &quot;setting-read&quot; person in our group) and who tend to fill the loremaster / tactical advisor of the party. I shy away from concepts of &quot;talented people&quot;, and my characters usually are hardworkers who earned their knowledge and generally focus on strategic approach to life and stuff.<br /> Making myself a character who knows 0 about the setting and relies on talents instead of refined abilities sounds like a cool break from my usual paradigm. +, I think it's a nice way to make my fellow players think little more than usual about their Orders and stuff, so they can explain them to my character and possibly recruit her :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:07:31-07:00","id":875110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=875087#post875087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently having a weird urge to make my first 2nd ED Mage character a classical genius newbie - a character who awakened week ago, but has Gnosis 2 (goodbye, 5 merit dots), no Order membership and literally learns the setting as we go in.<br /> I usually play characters with deep understanding of the settings (because I'm probably the most &quot;setting-read&quot; person in our group) and who tend to fill the loremaster / tactical advisor of the party. I shy away from concepts of &quot;talented people&quot;, and my characters usually are hardworkers who earned their knowledge and generally focus on strategic approach to life and stuff.<br /> Making myself a character who knows 0 about the setting and relies on talents instead of refined abilities sounds like a cool break from my usual paradigm. +, I think it's a nice way to make my fellow players think little more than usual about their Orders and stuff, so they can explain them to my character and possibly recruit her :P.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well you could always combine the two approaches as well - someone who is versed in the <i>wrong</i> lore. They think they understand how the world works, but they know nothing (<span style=\"font-size:8px\">Jon Snow</span>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:29:20-07:00","id":875136,"title":"","content":"Young neopagan is discovered by an elder of the Circle who mistakes her passing interest in pop occultism with a genuine rediscovery of the lost old ways and now has to deal with her new role as high priestess of the dark goddess. I especially like the idea of her being the first new childe in an ancient bloodline for a very long time, so she's tasked with representing an (un)living mystery to wider Kindred society despite knowing nothing about nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:30:35-07:00","id":875138,"title":"","content":"I recently read Beast, so I've been spending my free time thinking about a beast who winds up with an astral reflection of Father Wolf as their horror. He would hunger for all trespassers. Undecided what it would mean, cosmologically, for werewolves. Probably nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:57:46-07:00","id":875163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=875110#post875110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well you could always combine the two approaches as well - someone who is versed in the <i>wrong</i> lore. They think they understand how the world works, but they know nothing (<span style=\"font-size:8px\">Jon Snow</span>).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Character who tries to be genre savy but is missing the point every time she tries to use her &quot;it's totally like a game / fantasy show / dresden files!&quot; triumph card sounds like amazing Acanthus concept.<br /> So Amazing other people would probably strangle her after 30 minutes of playing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T05:06:17-07:00","id":875504,"title":"","content":"One i've thought about and find Silly but could work interestingly... A Mage that Follows the Jedi Code. Beyond that single line... Not much else to it.<br /> <br /> I've also wanted to play a Ordo Dracul Gangrel who's more a scholar then a typical Gangrel. Former Researcher/Geneticist, embraced directly into the Order... As the only way to cure his cancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:49:41-07:00","id":875756,"title":"","content":"A werewolf who used to be one of the cocaine cowboys in Miami during the 80s and has since used his drug money to found a mid-sized megacorp. He faked his death shortly after the first change in the 70s (His Miami drug career/ mega corp are under a fake name), but now has to deal with the fact that the son of his favorite younger brother he left behind is about to go through the first change too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:24:44-07:00","id":876051,"title":"","content":"In honor of the fact that Mage could be dropping any time now, here's a bunch of Mage ideas I've had, though obviously I haven't come up with normal names for them yet.<br /> <br /> \u2022Thistle<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> An Acanthus Th\u00e9arch, my idea for Thistle is that he was the son of people who were very powerful and very rich. He grew up wanting for nothing and eventually grew into a spoiled sybarite who flew from party to party and relied on mommy and daddy's wealth and prestige to get him and his fellow hedonists out of trouble... until one day he stumbled into a scandal that (while his parents were still able to suppress) finally made them decide enough was enough. On the threat of being cut off, he was sent off on a &quot;vacation&quot; to a small cottage in the English countryside, which led him to notice the strange things going on, which led to him grudgingly befriending the brownies that lived in the walls, which led to a thrilling adventure where... well, long story short, he grew out of his entitlement and fickleness and now burns with a subtle ambition to do something meaningful. In regards to the Arcana, he tends towards the Subtle, with a special focus on Fate and Mind, the later of which he'd likely make Ruling through a Legacy. My biggest issue with him is that I'm worried I wouldn't have enough Merit dots to fufill his concept.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u2022Brother Acheron<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A Moros Libertine, he was a pastor who over the years had become more focused on the trappings of religion rather than his actual faith, until his Awakening showed him what really mattered. Now he's stepped down from his position to not only work as a spiritual advisor to his fellow Mages, but to help the unquiet dead, who need someone to help them let go of the trappings that bind them to this world. He's taken to the study of the Arcana quite zealously, believing that studying them will bring him closer to God. He obviously focuses on Death, though I imagine he'd dip into Mind and Life (to diagnose and cure ailments both physical and mental) and Prime (for religious reasons). </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u2022Mutt<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Probably the one of these I've put the least thought into, my starting point for him was &quot;Wolblooded Mage&quot;. Currently I have him as a Thyrsus Arrow, probably with the Tell that grants fast healing. My idea is that he grew up poor, and still comes off as a touch rough around the edges, &quot;young, scrappy, and hungry&quot; as a popular musical might put it. A brawler somewhat lacking in social graces, he never the less bears a fondness for the low of station. By day, he works into community outreach programs to deal with troubled and impoverished youth, and by night he turns his Sight on the forces that would prey upon these people. His primary Arcanum would be Life, and his magic in general would focus on self-buffing and facilitating his fighting style of &quot;Punch it hard and fast until it stops moving.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T16:06:30-07:00","id":876078,"title":"","content":"-I need a good name for this character, but the gist of it is that they're an Guardian Acanthus (who pretty heavily practices Death as well) obsessed with reincarnation and the nature of the soul. In addition to being a topic I really enjoy in-game and out, it also gives me a chance to explore the aspects of the GotV that aren't just being the morally grey magic police, which never get enough attention.<br /> <br /> -While bordering on too tragic to ever be playable, Angel is a Galateid whose creator was looking for an ideal mate; when she insisted on her true identity, rather than the assumed gender of the body she was born from, she was cast out and forced to find her own road. Promethean is already a great game for telling queer narratives, and I'd love to focus on that even further.<br /> <br /> -Two other brief Promethean ideas: one scorned by a creator who assumed they were bringing a lover back to life and instead found a confused stranger in their body (exploring the story elements regarding how this body was not always yours) and a Hawaiian Extempore born from a volcanic eruption (showing off a non-alchemical, non-Western origin for one of the Created).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-14-2016, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T17:56:38-07:00","id":876141,"title":"","content":"An idea I've found interesting (if not one I necessarily want to play, because Guardians) is an Acanthus Guardian who not only sympathizes with the cause of Hunters, but believes that those who undertake the Vigil are worthier than normal humans, who play into the sleeping curse. They apply this belief by guiding and aiding them from afar, using magic and their resources as a Guardian to provide the Hunters with direction and supplies through drop-boxes, intermediaries, and Masques, occansionally using Sleepwalking Hunters as a deniable knife in the dark against Mages the local Consilium have decreed need to die. One of their more ambitious goals is to subvert the unaffiliated Cells in the area into a sort of Labyrinth (abet one where its members have no idea they belong to the same organization).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T18:47:50-07:00","id":876177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=876078#post876078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Two other brief Promethean ideas: one scorned by a creator who assumed they were bringing a lover back to life and instead found a confused stranger in their body (exploring the story elements regarding how this body was not always yours)</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds very similar to a Promethean + Genius pair I'd devised. They were previously husband and wife, but she was killed in a runaway experiment (which caused him to Catalyze). Desperate, he took up the offer of some stranger who could &quot;bring her back to life&quot;. And he did... except not. The Zeka that has his wife's body is not his wife with amnesia, but a whole new person. Dealing with that is rough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:06:13-07:00","id":884285,"title":"","content":"An Acanthus who takes Lawrence (of Arabia) as her Shadow Name, and is fresh enough to have not yet chosen between membership in the Guardians of the Veil or the Mysterium. She's fascinated by the Mysteries or North Africa and the Middle East, hoping to get out there and pursue her Obsession with the lost city of Ubar. She's an excuse to have a Mage focused on Mummy and Vampire crossover, and also to pay homage to the odd relationship between academia and espionage we see throughout the last few centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-06-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:26:53-07:00","id":884298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=866567#post866567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022&quot;Mr. Powers&quot;- Not sure what Incarnation, but I imagine him as a Inquisitor-Tempter. Whatever he is, his core concept is based around Show of Power and the fact that there ain't no rule that says you can't give Supernatural Merits with a Pact. I imagine him as a sort of &quot;power broker&quot;, giving out innate ability and magic items (Show of Power Gadgets) both to gain temporal power and because he believes he can find the secret to his own transcendence by studying how humans become something more and less than they once were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a sad person. I originally parsed this as <i>Austin</i> Powers.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't believe Vanessa, my bride, my one true love, the woman who taught me the beauty of monogamy, was a fembot all along. Wait a tick, that means I'm single again! Oh behave!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T01:07:17-07:00","id":886018,"title":"","content":"Osiris was dragged to a bloody corner of Pandemonium and suffered the lashes of devils, and from the scarred ruin of her self discovered enlightenment: the name, body, gender and all the other labels were just as much a part of the Lie as anything else. Now she's consumed with a burning need to storm her soul and tear off her dead name, to replace it with one of shimmering Truth carved on the world. Once she has tamed her body and made it the vssel she truly deserves, there's an obvious road to the heavens above that so desparately need to be rewritten. <br /> <br /> The old king dies and is dismembered; the pieces come together, lacking what makes them male, and now she is fit to rule the underworld as a god.<br /> <br /> (Mastigos with Life, Adamantine Arrow waging war on self-hate, carving a queer warpath across the Astral)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T18:54:37-07:00","id":888745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=876078#post876078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I need a good name for this character, but the gist of it is that they're an Guardian Acanthus (who pretty heavily practices Death as well) obsessed with reincarnation and the nature of the soul. In addition to being a topic I really enjoy in-game and out, it also gives me a chance to explore the aspects of the GotV that aren't just being the morally grey magic police, which never get enough attention.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps you could name them after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Santayana\" target=\"_blank\"><b>George Santayana</b></a>, who came up with the phrase &quot;those who do not learn from the past are doomed to repeat it&quot;. The Underworld is probably full of these people. You might need to switch the syllables around, use a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mondegreen\" target=\"_blank\"><b>mondegreen</b></a> or something like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T23:39:58-07:00","id":888895,"title":"","content":"A Changeling, probably Wizened Oracle, escaped from a True Fae with a fondness for mystery.<br /> He looks and speaks like a Sam Spade-style private detective, and his frailty involves falling into an overblown, gritty film noir narration at dramatically appropriate intervals, sometimes foreshadowing future events.<br /> He is somewhat disliked by certain members of the freehold aristocracy ever since one of his narrative attacks involved declaring the current ruler of the Autumn Court &quot;The kind of dame that brings nothin' but trouble,&quot; and going on a long tirade about her &quot;gams that seemed to go on forever,&quot; saying that he &quot;knew a lotta gals'd kill for a set like that, and, knowin' her, she probably had.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T05:46:42-07:00","id":889028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/863979-your-character-concepts?p=888895#post888895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Changeling, probably Wizened Oracle, escaped from a True Fae with a fondness for mystery.<br /> He looks and speaks like a Sam Spade-style private detective, and his frailty involves falling into an overblown, gritty film noir narration at dramatically appropriate intervals, sometimes foreshadowing future events.<br /> He is somewhat disliked by certain members of the freehold aristocracy ever since one of his narrative attacks involved declaring the current ruler of the Autumn Court &quot;The kind of dame that brings nothin' but trouble,&quot; and going on a long tirade about her &quot;gams that seemed to go on forever,&quot; saying that he &quot;knew a lotta gals'd kill for a set like that, and, knowin' her, she probably had.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone played this in one of my games. A little closer to Spades Slick than Sam Spade, and I think he was a Fairest Shadowsoul, but he would regularly narrate things out loud and not realize he'd done so until someone else pointed it out. Took a variation of the Vocalization derangement to cover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:06:15-07:00","id":889475,"title":"","content":"&quot;Numeric&quot; (need better Shadow Name)<br /> Acanthus Libertine<br /> &quot;I mean sure, everybody's happy to cry for revolution, but nobody ever seems to ask how we're gonna <i>pay</i> for it!&quot;<br /> <br /> Numeric sees himself as the voice of pragmatism in the Assembly. An accountant, he defies the stereotype of the flighty and fickle Enchanter by being a somewhat bland individual with a focus on practicality and common sense, using his skills and augury and prophecy to track the future and make plans as needed. His Techne focuses on finance and economics, using Excel and financial calculators the way other seers uses crystal balls and extispicy. Probably has Professional Training and focuses on Time, Fate, and Space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T23:33:49-07:00","id":890458,"title":"","content":"Tyr, a mage who Awakened whose backstory I'm honestly still hashing out. Fate has conspired to make him the local consilia's official liason to the werewolves, a duty he knows he cannot hope to escape. In the old legends, one wolf takes his hand and another kills him during Ragnarok, but he knows deep within his soul that he's safe until then. <br /> <br /> I've never played a character with a distinct destiny and it might be fun to explore that, especially as it relates to Shadow Names and how much occult heft they carry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T23:44:43-07:00","id":890460,"title":"","content":"A wolf blooded who was trained since he was a child to be the next great shaman. It was said that all the signs pointed to his destiny as a great shaman. They were right but they were wrong. He never underwent the first change but rather awakened. As a thysus mage he was determined to become the shaman he was groomed to be.<br /> <br /> He would be a shaman like none before him. This is a gift of Luna just like the change (flawed belief) and he will make the best use of it for his people as he can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T16:58:20-07:00","id":921231,"title":"","content":"Could a Beast run a haunted house attraction (like you see crop up around Halloween) and still feed from that? Because that might be hilarious, a Beast who feeds on giving people 'safe scares.'<br /> <br /> Failing that, one who does haunted tours would also be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T18:32:38-07:00","id":921272,"title":"","content":"A Libertine Mastigos with the shadow name Don Juan, whose Obsessions revolve around human intimacy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T06:12:29-07:00","id":921460,"title":"","content":"I've got two ideas for the Changeling side of Requiem for Regina.<br /> <br /> \u2022One is a Snowskin Fairest of the Snow Court. Taken to a plain of vast emptiness and freezing weather, he found comfort in God. Through this faith, he was able to endure long enough to chance upon other captives, and was able to inspire enough hope in them to help them all escape. Heavily focused on Resolve and Composure, he maintains a cold, passive air that hides a will of iron. For in the end, this too shall pass.<br /> <br /> \u2022The other is a Chirurgeon Wizened of the Ash Court. Raised among a wealthy family, he studied medicine in his books while hoping to someday work on a living person. His Keeper, a cruel creature of broken dreams, snatched him away and forced him to work on those injured irreparably without rest or succor in hopes of shattering his spirit. But in the end he improved his skill and escaped, now with a burning desire to practice not for fun, but to help others. He works as a street doctor, tending to the poor and his fellow Lost for little to no cost, no questions asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}